    {
      "id": "macbeth/sceneII_20.2/p@40144",
      "type": "speech",
      "tag": "p",
      "classes": [
        "drama"
      ],
      "text": "LADY MACBETH.\nThat which hath made them drunk hath made me bold:\nWhat hath quench’d them hath given me fire.—Hark!—Peace!\nIt was the owl that shriek’d, the fatal bellman,\nWhich gives the stern’st good night. He is about it.\nThe doors are open; and the surfeited grooms\nDo mock their charge with snores: I have drugg’d their possets,\nThat death and nature do contend about them,\nWhether they live or die.",
      "separatorAfter": "\n\n",
      "spans": [],
