    {
      "id": "macbeth/sceneII_20.2/p@42739",
      "type": "speech",
      "tag": "p",
      "classes": [
        "drama"
      ],
      "text": "MACBETH.\nMethought I heard a voice cry, “Sleep no more!\nMacbeth does murder sleep,”—the innocent sleep;\nSleep that knits up the ravell’d sleave of care,\nThe death of each day’s life, sore labour’s bath,\nBalm of hurt minds, great nature’s second course,\nChief nourisher in life’s feast.",
      "separatorAfter": "\n\n",
      "spans": [],
      "lines": [
