      "type": "speech",
      "tag": "p",
      "classes": [
        "drama"
      ],
      "text": "LADY MACBETH.\nInfirm of purpose!\nGive me the daggers. The sleeping and the dead\nAre but as pictures. ’Tis the eye of childhood\nThat fears a painted devil. If he do bleed,\nI’ll gild the faces of the grooms withal,\nFor it must seem their guilt.",
      "separatorAfter": "\n\n",
      "spans": [],
      "lines": [
